24:- **Generator-protocol freeze (isolates policy improvement):** for any policy comparison, the *entire* generation protocol is frozen and versioned — proposer prompt, direction-summary prompt, catalog-extraction prompt+schema, candidate ranking inputs, repair/unstick allowances, model IDs + efforts. Fixed arms run the **same protocol on their own admissible histories**. Any discretionary intervention outside the frozen protocol is logged as a **protocol breach**. The primary comparison is **assignment-retentive**: all assigned attempts, failures, and costs stay in their arm (no post-hoc exclusion of inconvenient outcomes). Exclusions are allowed **only** under predeclared, outcome-independent criteria frozen before the comparison. A breach that changes admissible information or treatment **invalidates the affected comparison** (restart requires appropriately unused evaluation evidence); logging/charging the breach never repairs biased inclusion. Only the executable **policy module** differs between arms.
